1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,360
I heard that
you also got into a university in Bangkok.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:06,960
I got accepted to the Faculty of Sports Science
through the athlete quota.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,640
Are you okay
with me going to study in Bangkok?

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:11,760
Of course.

5
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:16,400
I forgot that we couldn’t ride a bike
and play around forever.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,040
No matter where we are,

7
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,200
we will never be apart.

8
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:22,880
I promise.

9
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,560
Class, attention.

10
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you.

11
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,040
The class is over.

12
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,680
Let’s go have ice cream.

13
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:42,840
Sure.

14
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,800
Shall we go ride a bike at Koh Loi?

15
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:45,600
Ko.

16
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,800
Ko, wake up.

17
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,040
Ko.

18
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:50,880
Ko, wake up.

19
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,440
Ko, wake up.

20
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:52,960
Ko!

21
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,280
(I have this dream again.)

22
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:01,880
(I dreamed about my old days,
places, and people from my past)

23
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,640
(as if we had never grown up.)

24
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:10,480
(But the reality is we are growing up every day.)

25
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,520
(I’m well aware of that.)

26
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:17,320
(I also know that I’m not a high school kid anymore.)

27
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:46,200
(Bangkok scent, I can’t explain it in words.)

28
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,400
(But it’s certainly not
the ocean scent of my hometown.)

29
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,640
(The only thing that has not changed
is the man by my side.)

30
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,320
Can I have some too?

31
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,040
I already made one for you. It’s over there.

32
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,640
You really read my mind.

33
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,320
When are you leaving?

34
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,360
I was supposed to leave half an hour ago.

35
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:20,960
What?

36
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,480
Why are you still here?

37
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,960
You didn’t wake me up.

38
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,520
This is your fault.

39
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,640
So this is my fault?

40
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,960
I don’t want to go.

41
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:37,880
I want to hold you a bit longer.

42
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,280
Don’t be a baby, doctor.

43
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,960
If your patients saw you like this,
they would be upset.

44
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,520
Let them be.

45
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,000
I still want to hold my boyfriend.

46
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,280
Okay, I’m going to get ready.

47
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,200
I’m going.

48
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:06,000
(What’s up? Why are we having a group call?)

49
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,560
(My mom wants to know
who will come home for the New Year.)

50
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,200
(She needs to know the number to tell the caterer.)

51
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:10,920
(I’m going.)

52
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:13,440
(I already told Augar
that I will arrive a day before Achi.)

53
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,280
(What about you, Ko? Will you go home?)

54
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,320
(If you are going, I will clear out my car
and free up some space.)

55
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:25,840
Ko, Augar and August ask
if you’re going home for the New Year?

56
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,720
I have to check first.

57
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:28,760
I’ll tell you later.

58
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,400
I’ve got to go.

59
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,280
See you.

60
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,880
He has to check first.

61
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,480
Will he go?

62
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,320
(Why are you riding home with me?)

63
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,560
(If I had another choice, I wouldn’t ride with you.)

64
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,560
(I’ve never asked you to do it.)

65
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,480
(Why did you take Dad’s car?)

66
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:55,840
(If you ask me what hasn’t changed,)

67
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,600
(I’m a better driver than you.)

68
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,160
(I would say these guys.)

69
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:07,040
(August is busy with his capstone project.)

70
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:07,640
Professor.

71
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,680
I’m not sure about…

72
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:17,080
(Augar is a rising star of his team.)

73
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:24,840
(Achi, who attends a university away from us,
is busy with his research project.)

74
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,400
(My life right now?)

75
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,560
(Good looks are not a free pass.)

76
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,320
(I earn extra money from modeling.)

77
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,880
(But I’m still attending classes.)

78
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,760
From the latest case that I show you…

79
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:42,000
(Ko Song is now doing his ward rotations.)

80
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:46,680
(Now, there’s only a river between us.)

81
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,800
(I don’t get why I was so worried back then.)

82
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,120
[I arrived at school.]

83
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:09,320
[Tell me what you want to have for dinner.
I’ll buy it for you.]

84
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,240
Ko.

85
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,880
Why did you come to school so early?

86
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,920
My boyfriend has a morning class.

87
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,520
So I woke up with him.

88
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,680
Your boyfriend is a med student, right?

89
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:23,640
So he is studying at a hospital,
just like in the movies, right?

90
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,640
Yes, something like that.

91
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,840
How long have you been dating?

92
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,320
He must be busy with school.

93
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,720
It’s unlikely that he met you in college.

94
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,240
We’ve been dating since high school.

95
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,760
He was my next-door neighbor.

96
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,560
Damn, that sounds so romantic.

97
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:41,360
Don’t tell me that one of you has a tree
and the leaves fall into the other house.

98
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:48,120
Seriously, Ko?
That sounds like a movie script.

99
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,160
It’s true.

100
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:53,120
When I go home,
I’ll take a picture of the tree and show you.

101
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,560
Good. I want to see it.

102
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,000
When will you go home?
This New Year holiday?

103
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,680
Yes.

104
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,280
That’s why I can’t go to the countdown party
with you guys.

105
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,120
It’s okay.

106
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,040
You can come with us next year.

107
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:05,240
You should go home.

108
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,400
Are you going with your boyfriend?

109
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:12,720
I’m not sure.

110
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:24,440
You came home on time today,
exactly at 8 p.m.

111
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,440
I’m exhausted.

112
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,440
Are you hungry?

113
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,640
Yes.

114
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,440
I’m hungry, but also tired.

115
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:56,320
Can you feed me through a tube, honey?

116
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,240
Stop joking around.

117
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,960
Did you hit me over the tube feeding joke
or me calling you honey?

118
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,560
Of course, the latter.
Why are you calling me honey?

119
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,280
Why are you still feeling shy?

120
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,280
Everyone calls their loved one "honey".

121
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,440
But it’s weird.

122
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,320
It sounds cringey.

123
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,400
Okay, okay.

124
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,400
I’ll stop teasing you.

125
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,240
I won’t call you honey.

126
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,480
I’ll call you Orange. It’s much cuter.

127
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,400
That’s not bad.

128
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,000
Orange.

129
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,280
What?

130
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,920
Orange is cute.

131
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:47,000
What are you doing?

132
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,840
Are you bored?

133
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:02,480
I barely have time to be with you.

134
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,400
I get it. I’m not bored.

135
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,080
Don’t get bored with me.

136
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:12,880
Sure.

137
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,520
Will you go home this New Year?

138
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,880
I haven’t checked my schedule yet.

139
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,800
I’ll tell you tomorrow.

140
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:49,560
AROI

141
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,080
What’s wrong?

142
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,960
You are the one who told us
to meet at this restaurant.

143
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,360
But you don’t eat anything.

144
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,800
That’s right.

145
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,760
You make me lose my appetite.

146
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,680
I’m not hungry.

147
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,800
I just want to meet you.

148
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,360
Okay. Then I’ll go back to eating.

149
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,960
How can you eat?

150
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,720
Look at your friend.

151
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,680
He’s stressed about something.

152
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,600
What else can he be stressed about?

153
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,240
It’s always about Ko Song.

154
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:21,480
Is that true?

155
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,960
Okay, it’s obvious.

156
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,160
What’s wrong?

157
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,040
What are you fighting about this time?

158
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:36,200
He and I barely fight.

159
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,600
But that’s the reason why I’m feeling this way.

160
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:42,520
Why?

161
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:43,920
Because you don’t fight?

162
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,120
Yes.

163
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,960
Everything he says sounds reasonable.

164
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,680
I try to understand him.

165
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,120
He said he is busy.

166
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,640
When he gets home and falls asleep
without spending time with me.

167
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,720
I understand him.

168
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,880
But I secretly feel upset about it.

169
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,560
Are you and Achi fighting, Augar?

170
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:03,600
No.

171
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,480
Really?

172
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,760
No question!

173
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:12,440
Look.

174
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,840
Damn.

175
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,480
Let me see.

176
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,960
Damn.

177
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,440
Is this chat between a couple or a thesis?

178
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,560
Stop it, jerk.

179
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,360
We are fighting every day.

180
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,240
It’s either he’s mad at me, or I’m mad at him.

181
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:31,440
Because we are apart,
we always have something to fight about.

182
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,640
Then what do you do?

183
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,360
What can I do?

184
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,920
There’s nothing I can do.

185
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:40,280
So you just live like this?

186
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,680
Yeah.

187
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,040
So how are you going to go home?
Have you talked to him?

188
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,960
If you want to ride home with me,
I’ll clean out my car.

189
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,240
He said he will let me know today.

190
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:55,240
I’ll bet 100 baht. He’s not going.

191
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:56,560
Me too.

192
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,680
You guys are such jerks.

193
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,720
Why are you barely eating?

194
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,480
What’s wrong?

195
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,760
I had dinner with Augar and August earlier.

196
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,200
Where?

197
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,600
Samyan?

198
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,440
Yes.

199
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,440
I was going to ask you to join us.

200
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,440
But I thought most of the restaurants
would be closed by the time you arrived.

201
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,240
Augar can’t eat dinner late.
Otherwise, he will be scolded by his coach.

202
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,600
It’s okay.

203
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,920
We can find time to meet up with them again.

204
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,160
How about the New Year?

205
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,360
We can meet them if we go home.

206
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,440
Right, I was going to tell you.

207
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,720
I can’t go home with you this New Year.

208
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,360
I have to stay to help my professor.

209
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:11,040
I may have to work the night shift
on New Year's Eve.

210
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,320
Work the night shift?

211
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,440
You will be tired.

212
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:21,040
You should eat a lot to gain energy.

213
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,760
So you will have energy to study.

214
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,800
Eat this. It’s delicious.

215
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,040
Did you take out the trash?

216
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:01,920
Yes.

217
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,960
I also threw away the postal boxes.

218
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:06,760
Well done.

219
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,080
Of course.

220
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,080
Orange.

221
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:25,640
What?

222
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:28,960
You understand me, right?

223
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,600
Yeah.

224
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,000
Do you really mean it?

225
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:44,760
If you are not okay with it,
I’ll talk to my professor.

226
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,160
It’s okay.

227
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:51,720
If you swap your shift,
you will have to do an extra shift later.

228
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:54,520
It will be tiring to travel to see my parents.

229
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,640
If you have to work after you get back,
you will be tired.

230
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:06,880
Okay.

231
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,280
Let’s go to sleep.

232
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,000
It’s really delicious.

233
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,200
I want to try it. Is this a new restaurant?

234
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:33,040
You need to try it. It’s a secret place.

235
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,600
Augar. Achi.

236
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,040
Hello.

237
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,280
You bail on us again, Ko Song.

238
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,000
Yeah.

239
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,880
I’m really busy.

240
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,760
Sorry. I’ll take a rain check.

241
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,800
If you bail on us again, I won’t let it slide.

242
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,240
Come on, get in the car.

243
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:52,960
See you.

244
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,200
Good luck with work.

245
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,440
You’d better drive carefully.

246
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:06,400
Got it.

247
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,160
See you.

248
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,640
Can you put it away, Achi?
I’m changing lanes.

249
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,680
Can you hold it still? I can’t take a bite.

250
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:32,040
Can you hold it yourself?

251
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,640
Then my hand will get oily.

252
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,840
If my hand slips from the wheel,
we could be in trouble.

253
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:40,040
When the road was clear,
why didn’t you eat then?

254
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,360
You kept talking.

255
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,440
How hard could it be
to hold the skewer for me?

256
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:47,040
I’m afraid that it might poke into your eye.

257
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,280
Why would it poke into my eye?
I don’t use my eyes to eat it.

258
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:52,440
What if you suddenly make a turn
or hit the brake?

259
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,800
Why do I have to explain everything?

260
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,440
So you are sick of explaining things to me?

261
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,360
What’s wrong with you?

262
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,280
I’m sick of arguing about the same thing.

263
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,960
Yeah, the restaurant thing too.

264
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,920
[Don’t forget to eat something before you leave.]

265
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,200
[You didn’t get much sleep last night.
You could feel lightheaded.]

266
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,160
[I’m not sure if it’s edible.]

267
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:43,520
[I made it last night
when you were nagging me about my slow packing.]

268
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,120
I’m going to turn down the air conditioner.

269
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,120
Are you hot?

270
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,880
Sure. I’ll be fine.

271
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,360
Can you get the blanket at the back
and give it to Achi?

272
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,240
He probably feels cold.

273
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:10,600
I do this because you are here.

274
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,520
Normally, I would turn off the air conditioner.

275
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,840
Don’t you feel hot?

276
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:17,080
Of course, but Achi gets cold easily.

277
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,040
What else can I do?

278
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,720
It’s not that hot
when I turn off the air conditioner.

279
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:26,320
You guys are really fighting all the time.

280
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,520
I thought you were kidding.

281
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,680
This is how much we argue
when we’re together.

282
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,680
It’s worse when we are apart.

283
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,800
Aren’t you sick of fighting with him?

284
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:35,640
No.

285
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,040
It’s better than having no one to fight with.

286
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,480
It’s because we really want to be together.

287
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,520
You’ve grown up a lot, Augar.

288
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:56,680
Because I’ve grown up,
I understand these kinds of things.

289
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:15,800
Achi, move the seat for me.

290
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:16,600
Wait a sec.

291
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:27,600
Thanks for the ride, Augar.

292
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,240
Yeah.

293
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,960
Tell August to return my comic book.

294
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:33,960
You really hold a grudge about this.

295
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,960
See you later.

296
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:38,600
Did you bring your swimming suit?

297
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,680
Of course.

298
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,000
You should go.

299
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:43,800
See you.

300
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:44,480
See you.

301
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,760
Drive safe, Augar.

302
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:54,840
Ko.

303
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:56,880
Ko.

304
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,080
Mom.

305
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:03,640
I thought you would arrive in the evening.

306
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,440
I haven’t prepared a meal for you.

307
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:06,560
Augar gives me a ride.

308
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,640
We left this morning.

309
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,480
Is that so?

310
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,560
Where is Ko Song?

311
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,040
He didn’t come with you?

312
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,360
He has to work today.

313
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:18,200
That’s too bad.

314
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:20,320
I thought we all would be together.

315
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:21,720
It’s okay.

316
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:22,840
Let’s go inside.

317
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,400
Sure.

318
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:27,320
My son is a big boy now.

319
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,600
You’re clinging to me like a monkey.

320
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,280
(Back then we had only this silly phone.)

321
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,880
(But it was much easier to talk to him.)

322
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,800
Hey!

323
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:07,480
Let’s go out to eat. I’m hungry.

324
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:24,240
(I’m afraid to call you as often as I used to.)

325
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:26,200
(Because I don’t want to bother you at work.)

326
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:34,360
[SEND A MESSAGE]

327
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:40,160
[I arrived home. Have a great day at work.
Don’t skip your meal.]

328
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:49,000
(The scent of my house makes me feel so good.)

329
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,840
(No matter who I’m trying to be this year,)

330
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:56,360
(when I’m home,
the old me is slowly coming back.)

331
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:57,880
Ko.

332
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:00,400
(But something has never changed.)

333
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:02,280
(At least, my mom has never changed.)

334
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:11,160
Ko.

335
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:14,600
Can you go to the market with me?

336
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,480
Why don’t you go with Dad?

337
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,280
I want to stay home.

338
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,200
She wants to show you off to everyone.

339
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:24,000
Me? Why do you want to show me off?

340
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:27,840
My son is handsome and smart.

341
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:30,800
You also come to visit me
during the New Year holiday.

342
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:33,080
Of course, I want to show you off.

343
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,400
You want to show me off
because I came home?

344
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,280
Yes.

345
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:39,720
You came home.
It means you think I’m important to you.

346
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:43,560
In simple words,
who you choose to spend the New Year with,

347
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:46,280
it means that person is important to you.

348
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:49,800
That’s why I want you to come home
for the holiday every year.

349
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:52,400
Alright, let’s go.

350
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,040
He agrees to go with me.

351
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:55,440
We will be right back, Tiam.

352
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,760
Ko, don’t forget to go greet the uncle.

353
00:23:59,080 --> 00:23:59,840
Sure.

354
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:03,240
SRIRACHA MUNICIPAL MARKET

355
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:04,280
Mom, can we go home now?

356
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:04,640
No.

357
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:06,960
Hello, Sri.

358
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:09,200
This is Ko. Do you remember him?

359
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,360
He’s my son.

360
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,240
Hello.

361
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:15,480
It’s been a while since I last saw you.

362
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:16,160
Is this your son?

363
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:16,760
Yes.

364
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:17,480
Hello.

365
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:18,400
Hello.

366
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,000
Who is this?

367
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,200
This is Ko, my son.

368
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:24,800
Mom, let’s go home. Stop showing me off.

369
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:26,160
Wait a sec.

370
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:29,280
Right.

371
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:31,120
What?

372
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:33,680
Can you go buy this for me?

373
00:24:34,080 --> 00:24:35,400
Buy the things on the list.

374
00:24:36,360 --> 00:24:37,880
Okay, okay.

375
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:39,880
If we split up to shop,
we can finish shopping faster.

376
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:41,240
Don’t you say you want to go home?

377
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,320
I’ll buy fish.

378
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:46,520
PORK AND OFFAL PORRIDGE,
BLOOD PIG SOUP

379
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:51,960
Hey, Ko.

380
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:53,840
Hello, Uncle.

381
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:56,400
Are you okay? You are coughing.

382
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:59,400
I was wondering
if you guys would come home this year.

383
00:24:59,440 --> 00:25:01,200
I saw August this morning.

384
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:04,160
He said you guys would arrive today.

385
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,720
Achi arrived in Bangkok yesterday.

386
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:09,480
So Augar drove home today.

387
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:11,560
How are you doing, Uncle?

388
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:12,720
Are you okay?

389
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:14,040
Same as usual.

390
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,920
I’m getting older every day.

391
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:16,880
What are you doing here today?

392
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:18,600
Did your mom ask you
to buy groceries again?

393
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,280
Yes.

394
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:23,160
Here, Uncle.

395
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:24,040
What is it?

396
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,800
The list of my grocery order.

397
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:30,520
Though you are all grown up,

398
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:33,800
your mom still asks you
to buy soy sauce for her.

399
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,400
Go see me at my shop.

400
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:36,920
Okay, Uncle.

401
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,840
I’ll go there when I finish eating this.

402
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,000
Ko.

403
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:48,680
When is your commencement ceremony?

404
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:49,640
You need to tell me in advance.

405
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:50,720
I need to rent a van.

406
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:53,280
It’s several months away.

407
00:25:53,280 --> 00:25:54,640
I haven’t graduated yet.

408
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,080
It’s not that far away.

409
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,200
It’s only a few months.

410
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,320
Watch out. It’s spilling.

411
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,680
I’m so excited.

412
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,320
I’m excited too.

413
00:26:02,760 --> 00:26:03,560
I’m proud of you.

414
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,120
Who is calling?

415
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:18,600
Hello. What’s up, August?

416
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,080
(What else could it be, Boss Ko?)

417
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,000
Hurry up and come here.

418
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,120
We’ve been waiting for you.

419
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:31,080
Augar and Achi make me feel like
a third wheel on the beach.

420
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,560
Damn.

421
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,440
(I’m helping my mom in the kitchen.)

422
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,320
You are not cool.

423
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:39,200
Why don’t you come
and help my mom clean the vegetables?

424
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:40,840
Then I’ll go to see Augar.

425
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:43,600
(Why would I do that?
It’s not my mom’s vegetables.)

426
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,800
Ko, you should go meet your friends.

427
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:47,360
I’ll help your mom here.

428
00:26:47,560 --> 00:26:51,680
(See? Your dad even tells you
to come to hang out with me.)

429
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:54,600
(Hurry up. Don’t forget
to bring your swimming suit, asshole.)

430
00:26:55,040 --> 00:26:56,040
Asshole.

431
00:26:57,040 --> 00:26:59,800
Ko, you should go meet your friends.

432
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:02,320
We will have the New Year dinner together anyway.

433
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:03,640
Right.

434
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,360
Okay.

435
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:06,800
I’ll go meet my friends.

436
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:08,000
I’ll be back when it’s getting dark.

437
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:08,480
Alright.

438
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:10,120
Go. I’ll do it myself.

439
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:10,760
Bye.

440
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:17,840
I’m doing it. I’m not slacking off.

441
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:30,920
Hey.

442
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:34,960
Are you Ko?

443
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,160
Yes, it’s me.

444
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:41,200
I’m a relative of the former owner of this house.

445
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:42,840
I moved here two years ago.

446
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,560
I went to visit my relative in another province.

447
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,400
So we didn’t meet last time.

448
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:48,240
You’re Ko’s relative?

449
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:49,520
Yes.

450
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:52,280
His dad wanted to sell this house.

451
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,920
But Ko asked him not to do that.

452
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:55,240
He liked this house.

453
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:57,560
I have to travel a lot.

454
00:27:58,040 --> 00:27:59,720
So I don’t have time to water the trees.

455
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:02,480
I’m lucky that your parents help take care of them.

456
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:04,800
Otherwise, they would have been dead.

457
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:08,320
Ko really likes the orange tree.

458
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:10,680
He asked me to take good care of it.

459
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:13,920
I like it too.

460
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,720
When I was young, I always picked oranges
from the tree to eat.

461
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:20,800
If it bears fruit, I’ll pick and give them to you.

462
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:24,920
I’ve got to go.

463
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:27,040
Don’t forget to say hi to him for me.

464
00:28:28,520 --> 00:28:29,800
Say hi to who?

465
00:28:56,880 --> 00:28:59,600
♪ Will say "I love you" ♪

466
00:29:01,600 --> 00:29:05,200
♪ Will say "I love you" so you know ♪

467
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:10,320
♪ No more watching from afar, letting chances go ♪

468
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:13,040
♪ Will say "I love you" so you know ♪

469
00:29:13,560 --> 00:29:16,400
♪ To make this worth the wait after all ♪

470
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:26,240
Argh!

471
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:26,760
Stop it.

472
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:47,280
You are late.

473
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,040
Why don’t you join them?

474
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:51,800
No, I don’t want to get wet.

475
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:56,840
How did you end up coming?

476
00:29:57,640 --> 00:29:58,920
Didn’t you say you had to work?

477
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:02,920
Yes, I had to work, but I found a way.

478
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:11,800
What’s going on with you two?

479
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:13,760
You are living together.

480
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:17,800
But you two look really worried.

481
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:34,720
I’m not sure if I made a mistake choosing a med school.

482
00:30:37,480 --> 00:30:40,120
I feel like I always leave him alone.

483
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:42,440
What makes you think that?

484
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:49,560
I always ask him if he’s okay.

485
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:51,480
He always says he’s okay.

486
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:53,360
But I don’t know if he means what he says

487
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:55,400
or if he said that so I won’t be worried.

488
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,360
I wanted to ask him that,

489
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,520
but I was afraid that we would end up fighting.

490
00:31:03,120 --> 00:31:06,760
Your problem is that you don’t say what is on your mind.

491
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:09,760
That’s why you keep worrying about things.

492
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:12,080
If I were living with Achi,

493
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:16,480
I would do everything
to make our relationship as good as it can be

494
00:31:17,760 --> 00:31:18,680
Trust me.

495
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,600
It’s not that hard to talk to him.

496
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:23,240
Compared to being apart.

497
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:32,560
Damn.

498
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:35,520
Longing is like a double-edged sword.

499
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,440
I’m so sad that I can’t see Achi.

500
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:42,280
But I’m glad that it makes me realize…

501
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,880
how much I love him.

502
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:53,440
To tell you the truth.

503
00:31:54,600 --> 00:31:56,200
I’ve never felt that we are apart.

504
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:59,200
You two are living together

505
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:04,040
Don’t let things drift you apart.

506
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:26,360
Augar.

507
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:27,960
Augar.

508
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:29,200
Augar.

509
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:32,480
Ko Neung threw sand into my eye.

510
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:33,800
Which one?

511
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:35,720
The right eye.

512
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:38,200
It’s out.

513
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,240
What are you doing?

514
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:06,280
Happy New Year.

515
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:07,240
Happy New Year.

516
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:08,480
Here is your food.

517
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:09,920
Hello.

518
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:10,840
Damn, this is so cool.

519
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:12,920
Make yourself at home

520
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:16,640
I didn’t even know that they prepared this.

521
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:20,480
What should I do if my mom does this too?

522
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:22,720
Come on.

523
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:24,520
The adults want to celebrate.

524
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:25,840
Don’t think too much about it.

525
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:28,200
Just let them do whatever they want.

526
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:29,640
Hello, hello.

527
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:30,640
Hello.

528
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:37,960
Everyone, today is a good day to celebrate the New Year.

529
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:48,560
I also want to celebrate Ko and his friends’ graduation.

530
00:33:51,520 --> 00:33:53,720
No, one of us hasn’t graduated yet.

531
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:56,400
He has two years left.

532
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:58,640
That’s right.

533
00:33:59,080 --> 00:34:01,120
He’s a med student.

534
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:02,800
It’s okay.

535
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:05,720
Let’s celebrate for him in advance.

536
00:34:06,160 --> 00:34:06,800
Alright.

537
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:10,600
Ko, come here and sing.

538
00:34:13,840 --> 00:34:14,960
Yeah, both of you.

539
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:15,720
Come on.

540
00:34:16,200 --> 00:34:16,960
Come on.

541
00:34:18,880 --> 00:34:21,960
